<title>USA: U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA wheat export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net sales of 275,100 metric tons (MT) were 42 percent below the previous week and one-third under the 4-week average. Major increases reported for Taiwan (80,900 MT), the Philippines (52,900 MT), Japan (42,800 MT), Venezuela (36,200 MT), and Mexico (36,200 MT) were partly offset by decreases for unknown destinations (36,000 MT).</p>
<p>Exports of 420,200 MT were 13 percent lower than the week earlier and 23 percent less than the 4-week average.  The primary destinations were Sri Lanka (48,000 MT), Slovenia (38,800 MT), Thailand (35,000 MT), Israel (34,400 MT), Pakistan (31,500 MT), and Yemen (31,500 MT).</p>
</text>
